# Change control: a shared category of what a change-management process
# must do, in the spirit of common change-management objectives (ITIL
# change enablement, the change-management criteria of SOC 2). A sketch
# for onto's functor demos: it is not the text of any standard and does
# not certify anything.
#
# Organizations map their own policy into it with a functor
# (`docs/05-functors.md`); the functor's report is the gap analysis.

category ChangeControl {
    capability Approval { issuers: authorize; }

    objects: Requested, Classified, Verified, Authorized, Implemented, Reviewed;

    about Verified: "the change was tested, security-reviewed, and its back-out rehearsed";

    classify:    Requested -> Classified   "the kind and the risk of the change are recorded";
    verify:      Classified -> Verified    "the change is tested, security-reviewed and its back-out rehearsed before it is authorized";
    authorize:   Verified -> Authorized    "an authority approves the change" ensures Approval;
    implement:   Authorized -> Implemented "the change is put into production";
    post_review: Implemented -> Reviewed   "a post-implementation review is recorded";

    entry Implemented: needs Approval;
    invariant via: Requested -> Implemented through Verified;
    invariant via: Requested -> Implemented through Authorized;
}
